{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1394209-on-the-a-touch-of-spirit-optional-rule-from-how-do-you-do-that","id":1394209,"title":"On the \"A Touch of Spirit\" optional rule from 'How Do You DO That?'","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-04T18:46:46-07:00","id":1394209,"title":"On the \"A Touch of Spirit\" optional rule from 'How Do You DO That?'","content":"According to &quot;How Do You DO That?&quot;, a mage whose paradigm reflects connecting to certain Spiritual essences can add Spirit 2 to a spell to reflect this connection, as well as Mind 2 to certain Effects to reflect 'psychic empowerment' and the like. Now my question is, what real benefits do these added Spheres provide? As written, they only seem to be there to provide justification for certain paradigm effects.<br /> <br /> My theory is that, if these optional rules are to be included, they could be used either to A). influence the counterspell rules by providing an alternate foundation to the spell (shaman growing fangs/claws by connecting to Wolf spirit [Life 3/Spirit 2] is dispelled by knowing a dot in Spirit, not in Life); or B). gives some extra support to the effect in question, thus allowing the Effect at a lower rank (our afore-mentioned Wolf-channeler grows his fangs at Life 2/Spirit 2 instead of at Life 3).<br /> <br /> Anyone have any comments, critiques, or additional thoughts on this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T19:01:37-07:00","id":1394210,"title":"","content":"As written, it's purely flavor with no system benefits: you do it because your Focus demands that you do it. Not that it's much of a demand, as mages who use this optional rule generally have the two dots in Spirit anyway; and M20 doesn't penalize you for throwing another Sphere into the Effect. <br /> <br /> The developers of MRev revealed once that they were intending to introduce the notion that a rote could let you access a particular Effect using an alternate spread of Spheres, along the lines of your second suggestion. I'm a little leery of that idea, myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T12:44:50-07:00","id":1394411,"title":"","content":"I think the optional rule is helpful because it can prompt a storyteller decide how they use spheres in their game. For example, when I run Mage, I use spheres and sphere level as a way to quantify the effects of a rote/ritual/spell. In my game, a mage who magically lights a candle is doing the exact same forces effect, whether or not they're calling on flame spirits, channeling the five elements with chi, focusing their pyrokinesis, or manipulating the ether with some kind of arcane geometry.<br /> <br /> Because my concept of the spheres is focused entirely on effect, divorced from practice, I obviously wouldn't use that rule.<br /> <br /> Other storytellers may look at spheres as reflection of methodology AND effect. To those storytellers, there is a substantial difference between a mage summoning a flame spirit and a mage using pyrokinesis, and the optional rule is one way to represent that.<br /> <br /> For players, I think the distinction is largely meaningless. Like Dataweaver says, any practitioner that the rule would apply to would probably already have those dots in spirit anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T16:41:08-07:00","id":1394450,"title":"","content":"It's a very confusing addition because whilst it posits it as an optional rule there's many rotes in the core and that very book that seem to have this weird sphere tax that only makes sense if you're using that rule- and even then it doesn't outright tell you that the rule is being used. <br /> <br /> The way I see it, it should make getting successes for those Effects easier. If I did Life 3 Prime 2 Spirit 2 rather than Life 3 for example, I should have a lower number of successes required. If the main benefit is just to inconvenience Unweaving, then it doesn't really feel impactful imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T18:00:51-07:00","id":1394918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Distant Choir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1394209-on-the-a-touch-of-spirit-optional-rule-from-how-do-you-do-that?p=1394450#post1394450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a very confusing addition because whilst it posits it as an optional rule there's many rotes in the core and that very book that seem to have this weird sphere tax that only makes sense if you're using that rule- and even then it doesn't outright tell you that the rule is being used.<br /> <br /> The way I see it, it should make getting successes for those Effects easier. If I did Life 3 Prime 2 Spirit 2 rather than Life 3 for example, I should have a lower number of successes required. If the main benefit is just to inconvenience Unweaving, then it doesn't really feel impactful imo.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think unweaving spells or counterspelling mentions you just need 1 dot of any of the spheres, though maybe I am wrong?, so if someone grew fangs using Spirit/Life, it would actually be EASIER for others to counterspell it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T22:49:27-07:00","id":1395006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1394209-on-the-a-touch-of-spirit-optional-rule-from-how-do-you-do-that?p=1394918#post1394918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think unweaving spells or counterspelling mentions you just need 1 dot of any of the spheres, though maybe I am wrong?,</div> </div> </div> </div>There are several ways to counterspell.<br /> <br /> * Having a Sphere of the target spell at 1 allows you to countermagick with a difficulty of 7. You can also only counterspell things that are targetting yourself.<br /> * If you also have Prime 1 and 1 Quintessence, you can countermagick a spell not aimed at you - but at difficulty 8 (to counterspell) or even 9 (to reflect it back, needs to overcome all successes)<br /> * Anti-Magick: You roll your dots of Prime, difficulty 8. Each successes increases the diff of the target to cast the spell by +1 (max +3) and each success costs 1 Quintessence.<br /> * Unweaving is the removal of spells that are already in effect, and it requires at least 1 dot in ALL spheres of the target spell. Base difficulty is 8. You need to beat the original successes.<br /> <br /> One thing that is not mentioned in the Countermagick section is the most powerful way of countering a spell:<br /> * Spell-vs-spell: If you have the necessary (or higher) dots in Spheres to ruin a Target's spell with one of your own (you have Forces 2, they toss a fireball and you use it to redirect it somewhere else, etc.) you not only get the advantage of rolling at standard difficulty for your countering spell, but it is also potentially always Coincidential - after all, it's the enemy's spell that is behaving weird, not yours. So, difficulty 5 to make the fireball fly into a wall instead of you. Of course you can't stop a Tsunami with Forces 2 like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T21:52:14-07:00","id":1395235,"title":"","content":"I always thought it was strange they never mention the fun way of countering: spells. The book never goes \u201cjust block spells avatar the last air bender style, stop a wall of fire coming towards you with a wall of water or earth\u201d or what you suggested. It seems like something that\u2019s be in a damn magic game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T23:26:25-07:00","id":1395251,"title":"","content":"Isn't it mentioned, not even in the body of the text?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T13:41:55-07:00","id":1395903,"title":"","content":"Do they not have Sphere vs. Sphere countermagic anymore? I'd have thought such methods would fall under that umbrella.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T05:54:18-07:00","id":1396002,"title":"","content":"Not mentioned at all as far as I've seen. I guess that's less of countering magic and more of lobbing a spell at another spell","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T17:17:58-07:00","id":1396082,"title":"","content":"I think that sort of thing is probably a matter of flavor text.<br /> <br /> Mage 20's core rule book basically just says that a mage can use the same sphere to counter an effect. Each countermagic success removes an initial success, possibly causing the effect to &quot;fizzle&quot;.<br /> <br /> But I think the exact form this takes is probably up to the player/storyteller. If the player wants to say that, rather than &quot;unmaking&quot; the fireball in the classic way, he's manipulating water from a nearby fountain to create a wall that blocks and douses the fireball instead, then I'd probably allow it. The practical effect is basically the same. Except that this method would be pretty blatantly vulgar, as opposed to a possibly coincidental unmaking. But if the player would prefer style over common sense, I'm not about to stop him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T02:42:56-07:00","id":1396141,"title":"","content":"I think the idea was more like block a Forces firebolt with Matter by putting a wall in the way. But There's no real way to do that without preparing to cast a spell as someone casts a spell at you. <br /> <br /> Also, I really don't see that as countermagick in the normal sense. The successes vs success comparison might be irrelevant when say, a Lazer blast is cast and a mirror is shaped that provides full cover or say a mind illusion is used to redirect an attack by changing the perceived location if the target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T04:56:59-07:00","id":1396354,"title":"","content":"So here is my case for &quot;A Touch of Spirit...&quot;<br /> <br /> Oftentimes when we talk about sphere formula, it's kind of in a white box:<br /> <br /> How do I summon lightning?<br /> <br /> Oh, forces 3, perhaps prime if you want to summon it from nothing.<br /> <br /> But notice the question didn't mention anything about the character's focus, or paradigm, or anything. But suppose I have a character that believes in the power of dreams, and last night he had a dream about a thunderstorm. &quot;I want to reach into my mind, into my thunderstorm dream, and pull out the lightning!&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, we have Forces... and now, oddly, Mind.<br /> <br /> Even though you don't really need mind to throw lightning around, the player effectively added mind to the required spheres because of how he described the effect: He wanted to reach into his dreams and pull out lightning.<br /> <br /> And the player can have a discussion with the GM about what level of forces and mind are needed, as well as prime (can a dream be turned directly into energy?) and it may turn out that mind doesn't really add anything mechanically to the lightning, but ultimately the focus is the important thing. And who knows, maybe this talent for turning dreams into reality may come in handy when they later run into some chimerical creatures...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T07:43:32-07:00","id":1396380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1394209-on-the-a-touch-of-spirit-optional-rule-from-how-do-you-do-that?p=1396354#post1396354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But notice the question didn't mention anything about the character's focus, or paradigm, or anything. But suppose I have a character that believes in the power of dreams, and last night he had a dream about a thunderstorm. &quot;I want to reach into my mind, into my thunderstorm dream, and pull out the lightning!&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, we have Forces... and now, oddly, Mind.<br /> <br /> Even though you don't really need mind to throw lightning around, the player effectively added mind to the required spheres because of how he described the effect: He wanted to reach into his dreams and pull out lightning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eeeh, not really, IMO. As the casting in Mage is all process-based, I think it would still be Forces, because they are not literally pulling the lightning out of their dream. It still gets created out of nothing from Quintessence with the Prime sphere, even if they are actively *remembering the dream* and *think* they are pulling it out.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, that said...that character could *substitute* Prime with Mind <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> *Then* we have a mechanical difference in how the lightning actually gets created. With a twist, too, because in that case, they literally pull the lightning out of their dream and toss it at the enemy - but the lightning is then gone from their dream. They can't remember it in the dream because...it is literally, actually gone from there.<br /> It is essentially a pattern transformation from mind to forces.<br /> <br /> Such things are best handled with care though, else players get the idea of just 'thinking of' things before turning that thought into a pattern. Though on the other hand them permanently forgetting a thing actually exists when they botch is an interesting twist...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T10:27:00-07:00","id":1396426,"title":"","content":"I personally have no problem with a player adding in as many additional Spheres as they wish above and beyond the minimum requirements imposed by the rules, as long as none of the self-imposed Sphere requirements exceed the highest by-the-rules Sphere requirement: no harm, no foul. And even that condition is more a matter of \u201cwhy would you want to do that?\u201d, making it self-regulating. <br /> <br /> But once you start getting into the realm of self-imposed Sphere requirements <i>replacing</i> requirements imposed by the rules as written, you need to be very careful if you allow it at all. My own rule of thumb is that if you're using one Sphere to replace another that would technically be a more natural fit, then in addition to the usual requirements of having a paradigm-based explanation for why you can do it you should also upgrade what kind of Feat the Effect counts as, and thus how many successes you need to achieve to get it to work. <br /> <br /> For example, the Progenitor Focus allows them to view the mind as a manifestation of biological processes in the brain, which allows them to mess with cognitive processed like memory or perception using Life instead of Mind. But while it's something they <i>can</i> do, it's not something that Life is ideally suited for; so something that would be a Simple Feat for someone with sufficient dots in Mind will find it to be a Standard or Difficult Feat if he tries to do it by using Life to mess with the brain chemistry. (Conversely, a Verbena's view of how magick works generally doesn't involve the notion of brain chemistry and wouldn't allow for Life to substitute for Mind.)<br /> <br /> My rule of thumb is to double or triple the number of successes needed for the basic Effect if you're using something other than the officially prescribed Sphere, with double being the usual cost and triple being the cost if I think the player's rationale is questionable (but not so questionable that I'd outright forbid it). <br /> <br /> Conversely, if the Progenitor has sufficient dots in Mind to work there desired Effect, but wants to toss in a couple of dots of Life on top of that \u201cbecause it's ultimately just brain chemistry\u201d, he can; and the severity of the Feat doesn't change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T14:32:40-07:00","id":1396495,"title":"","content":"(I think HDYDT suggests being able to use Life 3 [I think] to be able to fuck with someones brain chemistry, but not outright mind effects. So Life ----&gt; Mind works rather 1-1 in some cases. I think you can use life to boost your mental capacities as well, I think Mind can do that as well?, so some things work better than others)<br /> <br /> Otherwise I agree. It gets kinda weird, because if my character thinks he is doing 'Matter based alchemy' (This gets more problematic the more meta you get) but I make fire with it, am I using forces or what.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T21:30:59-07:00","id":1396606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1394209-on-the-a-touch-of-spirit-optional-rule-from-how-do-you-do-that?p=1396380#post1396380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eeeh, not really, IMO. As the casting in Mage is all process-based, I think it would still be Forces, because they are not literally pulling the lightning out of their dream. It still gets created out of nothing from Quintessence with the Prime sphere, even if they are actively *remembering the dream* and *think* they are pulling it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... except they are, actually- what is a mage if not someone who bends reality according to their will? If they make the arete roll, what they say happens actually happens. *shrug*<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T03:42:33-07:00","id":1396639,"title":"","content":"I'd consider creating lightning from nothing, pulling it from ambient electromagnetic energies, and crafting it from one's imagination 3 different effects (likely with different sphere requirements) with almost identical outcomes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T04:44:36-07:00","id":1396644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1394209-on-the-a-touch-of-spirit-optional-rule-from-how-do-you-do-that?p=1396606#post1396606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well... except they are, actually- what is a mage if not someone who bends reality according to their will? If they make the arete roll, what they say happens actually happens. *shrug*</div> </div> </div> </div>I can give you a simple example of something a Mage might *think* they are doing, but they actually are not, and it's directly related to what we're talking about <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> &quot;Create something from nothing&quot;.<br /> <br /> As in, literally absolutely nothing. It's always the conversion of 'something' into 'something else' even if the Mage doesn't think of it - be it Quintessence, or using a different energy as a source like Spacecat mentioned, or..well, literally pulling a lightning out of your dreams. As I said, you can use Mind 3 to do that, technically, sure! But when you pull the lightning out of your imagination/dreams, it is gone from your imagination or dreams. It literally isn't there anymore because you converted it from the dreamstate into literal lightning in physical reality.<br /> <br /> Now you can say &quot;No, the lightning is still in their dream, they are just using the dream metaphysically as a template for the lightning&quot;, then...I guess yes, they can use Forces + Mind + Prime, but it would still essentially then be Prime-to-Forces conversion, just with the Mind sphere added, I guess.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T17:05:01-07:00","id":1396754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1394209-on-the-a-touch-of-spirit-optional-rule-from-how-do-you-do-that?p=1396426#post1396426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally have no problem with a player adding in as many additional Spheres as they wish above and beyond the minimum requirements imposed by the rules, as long as none of the self-imposed Sphere requirements exceed the highest by-the-rules Sphere requirement: no harm, no foul. And even that condition is more a matter of \u201cwhy would you want to do that?\u201d, making it self-regulating.<br /> <br /> But once you start getting into the realm of self-imposed Sphere requirements <i>replacing</i> requirements imposed by the rules as written, you need to be very careful if you allow it at all. My own rule of thumb is that if you're using one Sphere to replace another that would technically be a more natural fit, then in addition to the usual requirements of having a paradigm-based explanation for why you can do it you should also upgrade what kind of Feat the Effect counts as, and thus how many successes you need to achieve to get it to work.<br /> <br /> For example, the Progenitor Focus allows them to view the mind as a manifestation of biological processes in the brain, which allows them to mess with cognitive processed like memory or perception using Life instead of Mind. But while it's something they <i>can</i> do, it's not something that Life is ideally suited for; so something that would be a Simple Feat for someone with sufficient dots in Mind will find it to be a Standard or Difficult Feat if he tries to do it by using Life to mess with the brain chemistry. (Conversely, a Verbena's view of how magick works generally doesn't involve the notion of brain chemistry and wouldn't allow for Life to substitute for Mind.)<br /> <br /> My rule of thumb is to double or triple the number of successes needed for the basic Effect if you're using something other than the officially prescribed Sphere, with double being the usual cost and triple being the cost if I think the player's rationale is questionable (but not so questionable that I'd outright forbid it).<br /> <br /> Conversely, if the Progenitor has sufficient dots in Mind to work there desired Effect, but wants to toss in a couple of dots of Life on top of that \u201cbecause it's ultimately just brain chemistry\u201d, he can; and the severity of the Feat doesn't change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Infinite Tapestry also allows a mage to gain insights into the interrelation of Time/Correspondence and Forces/Matter via visits to the High Umbra, hence being able to use those Spheres interchangeably. Naturally this would only work with a Technocratic or technomantic focus ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T23:02:48-07:00","id":1396824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1394209-on-the-a-touch-of-spirit-optional-rule-from-how-do-you-do-that?p=1396644#post1396644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can give you a simple example of something a Mage might *think* they are doing, but they actually are not, and it's directly related to what we're talking about <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> &quot;Create something from nothing&quot;.<br /> <br /> As in, literally absolutely nothing. It's always the conversion of 'something' into 'something else' even if the Mage doesn't think of it - be it Quintessence, or using a different energy as a source like Spacecat mentioned, or..well, literally pulling a lightning out of your dreams. As I said, you can use Mind 3 to do that, technically, sure! But when you pull the lightning out of your imagination/dreams, it is gone from your imagination or dreams. It literally isn't there anymore because you converted it from the dreamstate into literal lightning in physical reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point. In a way, Mage doesn't actually allow true ex nihilo effects. It tells you it does, it says &quot;you need prime&quot; and then it tells you &quot;Oh, by the way, you aren't really making something out of nothing, you are really just using quintessence.&quot; Which is a slight bait n' switch but I am not complaining.<br /> <br /> I suppose if I had a player say &quot;I want to create lightning out of nothing!&quot; and I say, &quot;Okay, you need Forces 3 and Prime 2&quot; and he said &quot;No, I don't want to make lightning out of quintessence, I want to make it out of NOTHING!&quot; I would probably still require Prime 2 for game balance reasons, and maybe even throw on some level of Entropy or maybe a really high level of Prime to represent this refusal to work with quintessence and make lightning anyway. But then, everything is made out of quintessence so if he made lightning without quintessence... But he said he did it without using quintessence, and I have to be true to the effect as described... Ah! My head hurts! Make it stop!<br /> <br /> In all actuality I would probably talk to such a player about their paradigm and ask them to work some lore-friendly understanding of prime into it so I don't turn into one of those robots from the old sci-fi movies that self destructs when you ask it about love.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1078,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","user":"Froggy711","date":". 06-16-2020, 02:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T06:47:24-07:00","id":1397082,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I think that the player really needs to understand that they're forming something from quintessence vs. conjuring something from nothing, any more than a faith healer really needs to understand the anatomy of her patient when she prays to the Lord to heal him. The Consensus can say what it likes about cellular regeneration, muscle tissue damage, torn blood vessels and so on, but does she really need to know that stuff to make an effective prayer?<br /> <br /> (For that matter, a faith healer might say she's praying to the Lord to heal someone, but we're still requiring her to have the requisite points spent in Life, and we're still requiring her to roll arete.)<br /> <br /> Obviously having the prime sphere is an indicator that the Mage knows, or thinks she knows, something about the nature of the universe. But what does that really mean? And is there functionally a difference between creating an object &quot;from nothing&quot; and creating an object &quot;from the ether&quot; or creating an object &quot;out of thin air&quot;, or creating an object &quot;out of the fundamental nature of reality itself.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you're transforming an item out of ether/atoms/thin air/the innate substance of the universe, something that can't truly be measured or perceived in any real substantial fashion, then is that really any different from creating something &quot;from nothing&quot;?<br /> <br /> That's probably a storyteller call, but for me, it really isn't. What matters, IMO, is the strength of the Mage's belief, not necessarily her &quot;accuracy&quot;. As long as she has an understanding of &quot;how&quot; she's doing what she's doing (perhaps she perceives Prime as a divine act of creation, using the substance of God himself), then I think she ought to be able to do it.<br /> <br /> ETA: Actually, it occurs to me that the easiest compromise might just be to ask the player to tell you how the character defines &quot;nothing&quot;. Because I think most characters would have the idea that the universe is made of SOMETHING, whether we're talking about particles and waves or ether or divine energy or light (in the &quot;Let there be light&quot; fashion.) And that's what they're using when they're creating something &quot;out of nothing&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":". 06-17-2020, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T07:02:05-07:00","id":1397084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1394209-on-the-a-touch-of-spirit-optional-rule-from-how-do-you-do-that?p=1397082#post1397082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure I think that the player really needs to understand that they're forming something from quintessence vs. conjuring something from nothing, any more than a faith healer really needs to understand the anatomy of her patient when she prays to the Lord to heal him. The Consensus can say what it likes about cellular regeneration, muscle tissue damage, torn blood vessels and so on, but does she really need to know that stuff to make an effective prayer?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so - and it's also why I have an issue with the &quot;Do you EVEN know what you are doing?&quot; entry in M20 regarding a Mage having to know every little detail about what they are trying to achieve (i.e. conjuring a complicated machine, classic medicine skill to heal somebody etc. etc.).<br /> <br /> I personally think it depends on the type of Mage - a Faith based Mage, as you said, does not need to know details about a blessed sword they are calling for, or a miracle to heal a certain person. A Technocrat that tries to perform a healing with a jury-rigged tissue generator? They do, specifically because the consensus is also partially their consensus, and the biological process they believe in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T07:36:25-07:00","id":1397088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1394209-on-the-a-touch-of-spirit-optional-rule-from-how-do-you-do-that?p=1397084#post1397084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think so - and it's also why I have an issue with the &quot;Do you EVEN know what you are doing?&quot; entry in M20 regarding a Mage having to know every little detail about what they are trying to achieve (i.e. conjuring a complicated machine, classic medicine skill to heal somebody etc. etc.).</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit, I tend to apply that rule only to things that I think would require a very specific understanding of reality. For example, a computer is a technological device that has a lot of components that work together according to our understanding of science. I do think it's reasonable to require a mage who wants to conjure a working computer to have an understanding of those parts and how they work in general to make it work.<br /> <br /> If their understanding of a computer is &quot;a magic box that glows and lets me send messages to other magic boxes&quot;, then they might actually be able to create something that looks like a computer, and may even act like a computer in a limited basis (based on what spheres the Mage has at his disposal), but is in essence just a really fancy art sculpture. A non-Mage user, or a software engineer, wouldn't be able to make heads or tails of it.<br /> <br /> I'm less inclined to use that rule on something like the human body, which has been around for a very long time, and people have had some (contradictory) ideas of how it works for about that long. As long as their understanding of the human body seems to fit what they're trying to do, then I'm inclined to go along with it. In a way, my players are punished by their specificity. If they tell me they want to heal their friend's gunshot wound by using the ambient life energy around them. I'd probably say &quot;okay&quot;. If they tell me they want to perform magical surgery to remove the bullet, then I would ask &quot;...do you know HOW to perform surgery?&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T09:42:23-07:00","id":1397316,"title":"","content":"It's very much a matter of Focus. As I see it, one of the differences between mystical Foci and technomantic Foci is that the former are driven by Willpower while the latter are driven by Abilities: that is, the key ingredient in technomantic workings isn't Willpower, but rather knowledge and technique. Officially, that's addressed by the fact that mystics get to Work Without Focus while technomancers don't; personally, I expand on that by having technomancers replace the \u201cWillpower caps Arete\u201d rule with \u201can appropriate Ability caps your highest Sphere\u201d: a technomancer will be able to boost her Enlightenment all the way up to 10 without raising her Willpower to match it; but if she wants to perform a Life 4 Effect, she'll need four dots in an appropriate Ability (probably Medicine). <br /> <br /> For a mystic, though, all that's needed is Life 4. If you want to enhance that with some suitable medical know-how, go for it! But it's entirely optional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T16:43:24-07:00","id":1397843,"title":"","content":"The Sorcerer's Crusade book had an interesting take on this.<br /> There was a Time 3 effect for the Order of Reason, level 3 effects were things they did without even knowing they are magic.<br /> They would push their bodies to the extreme to be 'peak physical condition'<br /> The results?<br /> Extra turns as if using Time 3 normally. The focus? Being tough and buff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T00:12:25-07:00","id":1397902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1394209-on-the-a-touch-of-spirit-optional-rule-from-how-do-you-do-that?p=1397843#post1397843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sorcerer's Crusade book had an interesting take on this.<br /> There was a Time 3 effect for the Order of Reason, level 3 effects were things they did without even knowing they are magic.<br /> They would push their bodies to the extreme to be 'peak physical condition'<br /> The results?<br /> Extra turns as if using Time 3 normally. The focus? Being tough and buff.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are certain Cultists of Ecstasy that use a similiar (Though not quiiite the same) kind of focus/instrument.<br /> Of course with the mythical background of &quot;Changing your perceptions and emotions changes your reality&quot;, but pretty much with the same way of going about it - one of the example characters from the CoX book is an extreme athlete. Once they get into the rush of working themselves out and pushing their body, the magick kicks in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T14:29:01-07:00","id":1398063,"title":"","content":"I just think its a good contrast between what we have now. I'm not sure what I think is the correct choice, a more meta &quot;You only OOC know exactly what spheres you are using&quot; or one more grounded in in character sphere understanding. The former allows you to use Time 3 leniently with just being 'buff' while the latter means to act really quickly you'd be using some Life effect, maybe mind as well to incorporate your body.<br /> It also gives us the 'add spirit 2 to everything for no bonus' stuff which I'm not a huge fan of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T15:01:57-07:00","id":1398070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1394209-on-the-a-touch-of-spirit-optional-rule-from-how-do-you-do-that?p=1398063#post1398063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just think its a good contrast between what we have now. I'm not sure what I think is the correct choice, a more meta &quot;You only OOC know exactly what spheres you are using&quot; or one more grounded in in character sphere understanding.</div> </div> </div> </div>My personal irk with going for an IC understanding of spheres is always...that that's not how IC traditional teachings tend to work.<br /> For Hermetics, they mostly do, yes - but they're also the ones that brought that Sphere Esparanto to the table at the founding of the Traditions exactly to make it easier to talk to each other - because each Tradition thinks so differently.<br /> All the other groups? While they might certainly categorize their magic and the world into things (because really, that's just a human thing we DO), it would not make sense for all the magicka practices, some hundreds of years old and vastly different from each other, to suddenly break up all their old systems and lines of thinking just to make their *internal* teachings also fit along that sphere categorization. Yes, the traditionbooks of course tend to explain how each tradition sees each 'sphere', but IMO that's also to make it easier on players.<br /> <br /> IMO a good guideline of how some internal tradition stuff might work is the Dark Ages Mage book.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 06-21-2020, 06:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}